1. Why each additional element?
    * 3 firewalls:
        One in front of the load balancer, one in front of each server.
        They filter incoming traffic and block unauthorized connections.

    * SSL certificate:
        Encrypts traffic between the user and HAProxy so data cannot be intercepted in transit.
    
    * 3 monitoring clients:
        One on each machine (LB + 2 servers).
        They collect metrics and send them to Sumo Logic so you can observe the health of the whole infrastructure.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. What are firewalls for?
    A firewall filters network traffic based on rules.
    It blocks unauthorized ports and IPs, and only allows legitimate traffic through, for example, only port 443 (HTTPS) from the internet.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. Why is traffic served over HTTPS?
    HTTP sends data in plain text.
    HTTPS encrypts it with SSL/TLS so that passwords, personal data and session tokens cannot be intercepted by a third party between the user and the server.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. What is monitoring used for?
    Monitoring tracks the health and performance of your infrastructure in real time, CPU usage, memory, response times, error rates.
    It alerts you when something goes wrong before users notice.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5. How does the monitoring tool collect data?
    Each monitoring client runs as an agent on its machine.
    It collects logs and metrics locally, then ships them to Sumo Logic over the network. Sumo Logic aggregates everything in one dashboard.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6. How to monitor web server QPS (queries per second)?
    Configure the monitoring agent to read Nginx access logs or expose Nginx metrics.
    The agent counts requests per second and sends that metric to Sumo Logic where you can set up dashboards and alerts.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7. Why is terminating SSL at the load balancer level an issue?
    Once HAProxy decrypts the traffic, it forwards it to the servers in plain HTTP.
    So traffic between the load balancer and the servers is unencrypted, if someone has access to the internal network, they can read it.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8. Why is having only one MySQL server capable of accepting writes an issue?
    All writes go to the primary. If it crashes, no data can be written until it recovers.
    It is both a SPOF and a performance bottleneck for write-heavy applications.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

9. Why is having servers with all the same components a problem?
    If the database consumes too much CPU or RAM, it impacts Nginx and the app server on the same machine, they compete for resources.
    It also makes scaling harder: you cannot scale just the database or just the web server independently.
